[[2047,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3238830\">7040G24</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238829\">7040G20</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238795\">7040A31</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238790\">7040A14</a></p><p>1. Unscrew the screws.</p><p>2. Disconnect the electrical connection.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Air mixing actuator</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3237150\">N81</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>3. Remove the motor (3a) releasing the outlet shaft (3b) from the\nflap driving pin (3c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018556.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the motor is not damaged.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Do not check the function of the\nmotor by connecting it to 12V. Test the system,  by means of Examiner\nor other diagnostic systems, at the end of the operation.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>1. Position the motor.</p><p>To make easier the motor shaft connection, reconnect the electrical\nconnection and rotate the motor by operating the control on the\ndashboard, until the lining up with the flap pin.</p><p>2. Screw the screws.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018557.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,16,"<p><a href=\"#/3238790\">7040A14</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238795\">7040A31</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238829\">7040G20</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238830\">7040G24</a></p>"],[2047,127,24,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3238857\">7045A10</a>\n                                           (driver&#x27;s side).</p><p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Disconnect the electrical connection.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Air mixing actuator</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3237150\">N81</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>Remove motor (3a) by releasing outlet shaft\n(3b) from the operating pin of flap (3c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018588.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,24,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the motor is undamaged.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Do not test motor operation by\nconnecting to the 12V supply. Once the operation is completed, test the\nsystem using an Examiner or another tester.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>1. Position the motor.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>To facilitate connection of the\nmotor shaft to the motor, reconnect the electrical connection and turn\nthe motor by operating the control on the facia until it is aligned\nwith the flap pin.</p></aside><p>2. Tighten the bolts.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018589.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,24,"<p><a href=\"#/3238857\">7045A10</a>\n                                           (driver&#x27;s side).</p>"]]